From abdecab70a2ffe6f79cc2358194567517e86cb44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:59:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: trophies in the lobby, one for each cup cleared

Nine trophy actors (ACTOR_TROPHY_FIRST on, rows added to both placement tables before the
party rows, so the existing actor ids do not move) stand in a row along the ledge above the
entrance pits, each placed only when its flag FLAG_ARENA_TROPHY_FIRST + cup (0x790 to 0x798)
is set. The first clear of a cup (ArenaSeries_Cleared) sets it. Cups are bronze (1, 2),
silver (3, 4), gold (5, 6), gold with a crown (7) and blue (the two side cups). The row
leaves the lane in front of the counters free.

The art is placeholder: scripts/gen-trophy-sprites.py draws spr_309 to 313 (16 x 32, one
picture, the field sprites' palette) at build time, like the opponent sheets; sprites.tsv and
layout.tsv get the rows. 16 x 32 because nine 32 x 32 sprites exhausted the sprite VRAM
cache (the first line of a message window drew as noise). No talk handler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
